{"id":"f24a90d5cfa36cd1","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-zfc-model-beta-model.md","title":"ZFC Model Beta Model","display":"df-zfc-model-beta-model — ZFC Model Beta Model","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-model-beta-model","aliases":["58-df-zfc-model-beta-model"],"display":"df-zfc-model-beta-model — ZFC Model Beta Model","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-bijective.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-model-beta-model"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-model-beta-model</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-model-beta-model — ZFC Model Beta Model"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9e70b896da231f4f\" href=\"?note=9e70b896da231f4f\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md\">../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md\">../batch18/58-df-bijective.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega)\">\\(\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M=\\langle\\omega,\\mathcal S,+,\\times,0,1,&lt;\\rangle\">\\(\\mathcal M=\\langle\\omega,\\mathcal S,+,\\times,0,1,&lt;\\rangle\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,\\omega\\times\\omega,\\omega)\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,\\omega\\times\\omega,\\omega)\\)</span> (fixed pairing function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R_X^\\pi\\subseteq\\omega\\times\\omega\">\\(R_X^\\pi\\subseteq\\omega\\times\\omega\\)</span> (relation coded by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\">\\(\\pi\\)</span>, defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WF}\">\\(\\mathrm{WF}\\)</span> (well-founded-relation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9e70b896da231f4f\" href=\"?note=9e70b896da231f4f\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md\">../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{BetaModel}\">\\(\\operatorname{BetaModel}\\)</span> (predicate defined below)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}beta\\text{-}coded\\text{-}relation} \\vdash R_X^\\pi\\coloneqq\\{\\langle m,n\\rangle\\in\\omega\\times\\omega:\\pi(\\langle m,n\\rangle)\\in X\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}beta\\text{-}coded\\text{-}relation} \\vdash R_X^\\pi\\coloneqq\\{\\langle m,n\\rangle\\in\\omega\\times\\omega:\\pi(\\langle m,n\\rangle)\\in X\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}beta\\text{-}model} \\vdash \\operatorname{BetaModel}(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal S,\\pi)\\leftrightarrow\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega)\\land\\mathcal M=\\langle\\omega,\\mathcal S,+,\\times,0,1,&lt;\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,\\omega\\times\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall X\\in\\mathcal S\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WF}(R_X^\\pi)\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists f\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(\\{\\pi(\\langle n,f(n)\\rangle):n\\in\\omega\\}\\in\\mathcal S\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(\\langle f(n+1),f(n)\\rangle\\in R_X^\\pi))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}beta\\text{-}model} \\vdash \\operatorname{BetaModel}(\\mathcal M,\\mathcal S,\\pi)\\leftrightarrow\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega)\\land\\mathcal M=\\langle\\omega,\\mathcal S,+,\\times,0,1,&lt;\\rangle\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,\\omega\\times\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\forall X\\in\\mathcal S\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{WF}(R_X^\\pi)\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists f\\in\\omega^\\omega\\;(\\{\\pi(\\langle n,f(n)\\rangle):n\\in\\omega\\}\\in\\mathcal S\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(\\langle f(n+1),f(n)\\rangle\\in R_X^\\pi))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The right side expands what the omega-model means by “well founded”: it has no descending sequence whose real code belongs to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal S\">\\(\\mathcal S\\)</span>. This avoids applying the first-order satisfaction predicate to second-order syntax.</li>\n<li>Satisfaction of a chosen second-order theory is a separate conjunct for downstream theory-specific beta-models.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md","status":"resolved","id":"9e70b896da231f4f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-well-founded.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../ba